I disagree.  Part of the fun of NetHack is its "realism."  Starving to
death is fine.  But most people barf copiously instead of die from eating
too much.  That's the change I made.  One now just usually barfs, but can
still die from eating too much.  (Like HARD off.)  The current usage of
the prompt *is* buggy.

Someone out there should try my dog-move trick to see how they like it.
What it does is prevent the dog from stepping in your path if you're 
walking. (Like any sensible dog would.)  It cuts out half the "you stop
to avoid hitting your..." messages.  And one of the best things is that
if you're fleeing in a straight corridor, your dog won't block you.
It wasn't my idea, but I love the change.  I *like* my pet now!

